  "description": "VUVKEE crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C160 H220 Dy10 N10 O50,4(C2 H3 N1),9(C1 H1 Cl3). From the CIF bond table, Dy1P (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2P (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3P (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4P (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5P (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy9 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy10 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy1Q (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2Q (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3Q (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4Q (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5Q (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy16 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy17 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy18 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy19 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy20 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.797-3.831 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 104.91-114.86°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C177H241Cl27Dy10N14O50.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
